{
  "summary": "Adds an `auto_outbound_mode` feature to the functional test framework and introduces a new functional test `p2p_outbound_management.py`. In this mode, the node under test opens outbound connections to addresses in addrman via a local SOCKS5 proxy that redirects them to controllable Python P2P peers or other test nodes. The PR also refactors `p2p_private_broadcast.py` to use the shared framework implementation instead of its own duplicate proxy redirection logic.",
  "problem": "P2P connection management logic where the node autonomously decides when to open and evict outbound connections lacks functional test coverage because functional tests usually rely on inbound connections or test-runner-initiated outbound connections (`add_outbound_p2p_connection`). Substantive features like opening extra outbound connections on stale tips, periodic block-relay-only feeler rotations, and network diversification across reachability types have had no end-to-end functional test coverage.",
  "evidence": [
    "Adds automated test coverage for several long-standing outbound connection features: extra full outbound connections due to a stale tip (#11560), periodic block-relay-only connections (#19858), and full outbound connection management with respect to networks (#27213) (PR description).",
    "Extracts and shares generalizable SOCKS5 redirection test infrastructure originally introduced in #29415, removing 101 lines of duplicate test code from `p2p_private_broadcast.py` (commit d8b30ad131)."
